I would like to apply to join the LLG, only for making my commentary be
official:
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=gadri:+an+unofficial+commentary+from+a+logical+point+of+view

Whether my application is accepted or not, I still want LLG to consider
inserting the commentary in the next version of CLL. This commentary
contains a theoretical basis of Lojban, and should be essential for the
Book.

As for the competence in the fields listed above, I think I am incompetent
for all of them. However, I don't know how do you estimate the competence
in those fields.

The above mentioned commentary may be a piece of evidence for my competence
in logic, and maybe the following video can be a piece of evidence for my
competence in philosophy. I made a video clip of my speech to philosophers
on "Lojban and Quine" in Japanese language. You can view the video at
http://youtu.be/lzqhNYCWKLo
You can also download the pdf file at
http://guskant.github.io/lojbo/lojban20131221.pdf

If required, I will prepare an English version, but I don't think I can
finish translation before the next meeting of LLG. The contents of my
speech are shown below:


00:00:17 Planned language
00:02:46 Loglan
00:03:40 Basis of construction of Loglan: Leibniz
00:14:07 Basis of construction of Loglan: Whorf
00:20:30 Lojban grammar
00:23:11 cakyrespa
00:28:30 Practical use of Lojban
00:29:04 Lojban proposition
00:31:18 Observative
00:32:22 Description terms
00:37:40 New definition of description terms
00:41:06 "Pegasize"
00:42:14 Suggested grammar for "pegasize"
00:43:43 Use and mention
00:45:12 Lojban and logic - second-order logic
00:47:15 Lojban and logic - third/higher-order logic
00:52:06 Lojban and logic - multi-valued logic
00:53:13 Lojban and logic - modal logic
00:54:20 Summary
00:55:28 Discussion - Russell's interpretation
00:58:16 Discussion - Expressive power of Lojban and Logic
01:01:04 Discussion - Strong/weak principle of linguistic relativity
01:02:04 Discussion - No language, no thought?
01:05:00 Discussion - Logic to Lojban
01:05:48 Discussion - History: terms to relations, multi-terms to binary
01:11:17 Discussion - Language and vague description
01:14:53 Discussion - Unification of expression
01:17:14 Discussion - Practical use
01:19:00 Discussion - Quine to Lojban?
01:21:48 Discussion - Which are Quine-like?

